{{also|line up|line-up}}
==English==

===Etymology===
{{deverbal|en|line up}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK|US}} {{IPA|en|/ˈlaɪn.ʌp/}}
* {{audio|en|En-ca-lineup.ogg|Audio (CA)}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|US|legal|&|law enforcement}} a physical or photographic queue of people allegedly involved in a crime, allowing a witness to identify them
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1999| title=Criminal Procedure for the Criminal Justice Professional |author=John N. Ferdico | page=498| passage=Before viewing the '''lineup''', each witness should be required to give to the officer in charge of the '''lineup''' a written description of the perpetrator of the crime.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2007|author=Jack R. Greene|title=The Encyclopedia of Police Science|publisher=Taylor & Francis|isbn=9780415970006|page=493
|passage=This innocent suspect is placed in a '''lineup''' with five fillers who look similar to that innocent suspect. Given this scenario, one may ask How many people are in the '''lineup''' because they fit the description of the perpetrator?}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2007| title=Criminal Evidence: Principles and Cases |author=Thomas J. Gardner, ‎Terry M. Anderson | page=264| passage=Foster was placed in a three-man '''lineup''' for viewing by the only witness (the manager of the office). Foster was about 6 feet tall, whereas the other two men in the '''lineup''' were about 5 feet 6 inches tall.}}
# A list of [[train]]s that are expected to cross over a specified section of [[track]] during a specified [[time period]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1958| title=Preservation of Competitive Through Rail Routes|author=United States. Congress. Senate. Committee on Interstate and Foreign Commerce| page=63| passage=It is recognized that '''lineup''' will not contain information as to all train and yard movements within yard limits.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1959| title=Hearings|author=United States. Congress. Senate. Committee on Commerce | page=85| passage=Except under special or emergency conditions, track cars are not allowed on the main-line tracks until the man in charge has secured a '''lineup'''. }}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1965| title=Awards 11851 to 11915 Third Division|author=National Railroad Adjustment Board| page=509| passage=When it is impossible to obtain a '''lineup''', track cars may proceed, using special care, as the way is seen or known to be clear.}}
# {{lb|en|Canada}} A line of people or vehicles, in which the individual at the front end is dealt with first, the one behind is dealt with next, and so on, and in which newcomers join at the end; a [[queue]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2005| title=Lean Six Sigma Statistics |author=Alastair Muir | page=285| passage=We have a simple business process that consists of two steps: people wait in a '''lineup''' then fill out an application form.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2019| title=Life Lessons from an Ice Cream Shop |author=Tamara Beth Olsen | page=| passage=I've heard that information before and try to remember to do that when there isn't a '''lineup''' of customers. When there is a '''lineup''' of customers, I don't feel that I have enough time.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2020| title=The Customer Service Your Customers Expect|author=Brenda Robinson, ‎Harley Robinson | page=| passage=As soon as I entered, I saw a '''lineup''' of about 10 to 15 customers.}}
# An [[ordered]] [[list]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2006| title=Short-Term Trading in the New Stock Market |author=Toni Turner | page=261| passage=Look at the '''lineup''' of sideways, up and down gaps, spinning top days, all bunched around the two-hundred-day MA. }}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2002| title=Understanding Artificial Intelligence|author=| page=| passage=At the University of Alabama, Robert M. Metzger's group synthesized a molecule that had an internal energetic '''lineup''' of orbitals, which varied depending on the polarity of the voltage applied to it. The '''lineup''' of orbitals was analogous to the rungs on a ladder.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2013| title=Electronic Properties of Semiconductor Interfaces |author=Winfried Mönch | page=109| passage=The electronic properties of contacts between two semiconductors or, as they are commonly called, semiconductor heterostructures are determined by the '''lineup''' of their band structures across the interface and the existence of space-charge layers.}}
# {{lb|en|sports}} Collectively, the members of a [[team]].
#: {{ux|en|The manager fielded his strongest '''lineup''' for the game against United.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2006|author=John Roth; Ned Hinshaw|title=The Encyclopedia of Duke Basketball|publisher=Duke University Press|isbn=9780822339045|page=369|passage=Elton Brand in 1998 missed 15 games because of an injury in the middle of the year but returned to the '''lineup''' late in the season, so he is listed as a starter here. The aim here is to list the '''lineup''' that was in use near the end of each season {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2007| title=He Teaches My Hands to War |author=Larry Stockstill | page=133| passage=Before any game, a team is usually quite interested in its opponent's '''lineup'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2022| title=Racing with Rich Energy|author=Elizabeth Blackstock, ‎Alanis King | page=75| passage=Rossi's five starts during the 2015 Formula One season were more like a tryout for the Manor Marussia team, in which he replaced Roberto Merhi for a few races in order to help the team decide what its driver '''lineup''' would be the next year.}}
# {{lb|en|baseball}} The [[batting order]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1993| title=Baseball: Play the Winning Way |author=Jerry Kindall | page=248| passage=More than any other batter in the '''lineup''', he can keep the inning going with a a base hit, and over a season he'll have as many at-bats as teh lead-off man and thus hit hard and often for his team.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2015| title=The Complete Baseball Scorekeeping Handbook|author=Andres Wirkmaa | page=70| passage=For example, as before, the leadoff hitter for the visiting team in the top of the first inning fails to come to bat and the #2 batter in the '''lineup''' subsequently becomes the initial batter in the inning. }}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2022| title=The Lineup: Ten Books That Changed Baseball |author=Paul Aron · | page=96| passage=That meant Howell moved from a weak-hitting '''lineup''' to a great-hitting '''lineup''', and players generally said they hit better if they had better hitters around them. }}
# {{lb|en|car racing}} The order in which race-cars are positioned at the start of a race, based on qualifying times.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2009| title=NASCAR For Dummies®|author=Mark Martin | page=| passage=A double-car '''lineup''' means the third-fastest car lines up behind the pole sitter and the fourth-fastest behind the car on the outside of the front row, and so on throughout the field.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2017| title=The Nuts and Bolts of NASCAR|author=Greg Engle | page=| passage=The '''lineup''' was then set fastest to slowest. }}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2021| title=Blue Ridge: A New Home|author=James Jackson | page=| passage=Next, Tuddy gave us the '''lineup''' for the next race, which would be as follows: Bud, Puck, Joey, Pepper, me, then Ty. }}
# {{lb|en|marketing}} The set of [[product]] [[option]]s available from a particular [[manufacturer]] or under a particular [[brand name]]. 
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2008| title=American Cars, 1960-1972: Every Model, Year by Year |author=J. “Kelly” Flory, Jr. | page=486| passage=The mid-size Chevelle '''lineup''' featured revised frontal styling and one new model, a Concours Estate Wagon that sported wood-grain exterior trim and a black-accented grille.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2009| title=Factory Man|author=James E. Harbour, ‎James V. Higgins | page=100| passage=If you look at its whole product '''lineup'''—cars, motorcycles, marine engines, lawn mowers , power generators, and so forth —Honda makes about 30 million engines a year worldwide.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2011| title=Exchange-Traded Funds For Dummies |author=Russell Wild | page=46| passage=If you decide that part of your portfolio should be in mutual funds, you can do a lot worse than going with T. Rowe Price's '''lineup''' of entirely load-free funds.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2012| title=Mastering the Stock Market|author=John L. Person | page=82| passage=Let's take another example in this space looking at Dr. Pepper Snapple (DPS), which has a strong '''lineup''' of leading brands, including Snapple A&W Root Beer, 7UP, Hawaiian Punch, Sunkist, Country Time Lemonade, and Yoo‐hoo chocolate beverage against Monster Beverage Corporation (MNST), the high‐caffeine energy drink maker.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2023| title=Game Changer|author=Jean-Manuel Izaret, ‎Arnab Sinha | page=193| passage=Starbucks has continuously reshaped its '''lineup''', tweaking its prices and introducing new offers like the Frappuccino, the Pumpkin Spice Latte, and the Oleato. These active adjustments to its '''lineup''' allow Starbucks to continue to deliver what customers need at prices they're willing to pay.}}
# {{lb|en|music}} The members of a music group at any one time.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2013| title=Majorlabelland And Assorted Oddities |author=Pete Crigler | page=36| passage=After losing half the '''lineup''', the band went on hiatus before reemerging in late 1991 with a new '''lineup''' of Goss, bassist Googe and the legendary Ginger Baker of Cream and Blind Faith on drums.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2014| title=Punk USA: The Rise and Fall of Lookout Records |author=Kevin Prested | page=79| passage=Honing the band's anthemic sound and stance, they relocated to Richmond and created a solid '''lineup'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2023| title=The Journey Of Pearl Jam — From Grunge To Glory|author=‎Zander Pearce | page=| passage=Throughout their career, Pearl Jam has experienced a number of '''lineup''' changes, and the band has had several members come and go over the years.}}
# {{lb|en|entertainment industry}} The acts performing at a concert or festival.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2008| title=The Humana Festival|author=Jeffrey Ullom | page=77| passage=As the festival grew and the '''lineup''' featured more daring works, collections exemplified trends in national playwriting rather than the producing director's personal tastes. }}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2010|author=Ray D. Waddell; Rich Barnet; Jake Berry|title=This Business of Concert Promotion and Touring: A Practical Guide to Creating, Selling, Organizing, and Staging Concerts|publisher=Billboard Books|isbn=9780307875006|page=121
|passage=Festival talent buyers can take one of several approaches in putting together their '''lineup'''. {{...}} [H]e was very concerned about putting together a talent '''lineup''' that resonates with music lovers.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2016| chapter=Folk on the Rocks: The Beat that Sustains| author=Julia Christensen| title=Care, Cooperation and Activism in Canada's Northern Social Economy|editor=Frances Abele, ‎Chris Southcott | page=116| passage=The annual festival '''lineup''' is guided in part by the festival's efforts to maintain a rough 50/50 split between northern and southern performers.}}
# The list of [[program]]s scheduled to be broadcast by a television station, or a position in that list.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1966| title=Activities of Regulatory and Enforcement Agencies Relating to Small Business|author=United States. Congress. House. Select Committee on Small Business | page=| passage=In the case of Quaker Oats, which brought to us a program called "Bewitched," for which we sold them the time at 9 o'clock Thursday, they selected a minimum '''lineup''' of $60,000, because that is the half-hour minimum '''lineup'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2011| title=Handbook of Children and the Media|author=Dorothy G. Singer, ‎Jerome L. Singer | page=| passage=Currently ABC's linkage with parent Disney has paid off on Saturday morning, with a 3-hour '''lineup''' of shows from Disney-owned studios. CBS has a Saturday-morning '''lineup''' of shows produced by Cookie Jar Entertainment and NBC's programming is produced by QUBO.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2014| title=Encyclopedia of Television |author=Horace Newcomb | page=1618| passage=First, it moved the original ''Mystery Movie'' '''lineup''' of ''Columbo'', ''McCloud'', and ''McMillan and Wife'' to the highly competitive Sunday night schedule and, as a fourth installment to this rotation, added ''Hec Ramsey'', starring Richard Boone as a turn-of-the-century western crime fighter.}}

